I had the same problem with my PC 64. Yes it was memory related. Make
sure all of your contacts in both the memory banks and cache memory are
clean. Test all the memory. 

My problem ended up being in cache. I had changed my settings to 12ns
and that is where my problem began. When I kicked it back down 15ns all
was well. Steve G. from DCGinc verified that some of these model boards
could only use a 15ns setting on cache even when the chips were listed
as 12ns.

hope that helps
jeff
