But a wrong pathname for the kernel file would not allow the system to
get as far as allowing users to log in.

Even PAM configuration errors are unlikely in this case, since the
failure is reported to occur later during the session, _after_ a
successful login. At least that's my reading of the problem report;
if on the other hand the phrase "can log in as root" does not imply
getting a shell prompt after entering the root password, I'd recommend
reading about those infamous Pluggable Authentication Modules and how
to configure them. Root logins tend to be disallowed on "insecure"
terminals, which shouldn't include the console or the serial ports
but...

I'd suggest rebooting the machine single-user and investigating.
Or, if non-root logins work normally, using the "su" command from
a non-root account. 



