It appears to me the locking problem is being caused ny the tagging
queue.
Using the same driver at work on an intel box I found certain drives
misrepresent
how many queue tags and the modes they will work in. 

try:
boot sda8:/boot/vmlinuz root=/dev/sda8 ncr53c8xx=tags:0,disc:n

I think this will give you a stable system then try loser restrictions.

the exact prameters may be found in:
/usr/src/linux/drivers/scsi/README.ncr53c8xx
