Linux on Alpha is 64 Bit, the 31bit limit (2GB) comes from the Drivers that
were written using the Intel model .ie. PCI bus DMA's were Directly mapped
to memory space. If they used Scatter/Gather mode as Digital UNIX does the
artificial would not exist.  These issues are being work and hopefully will
eventually make it into the 2.3 bit stream.

There are other limits on memory size currently coded into the generic
kernels based on system type. EV6 machines are all 2Gb, EV5.* &EV4 are split
between 1Gb and 2Gb. These limits were coded due to the driver limitations,
An effort was made not to use all the DMA mapping windows so scatter/gather
could be implemented later as the driver issues were resolved.

As for performance, when the "DIGITAL ALPHA compilers, Fortran and "C" " are
release for Linux, the performance gap will be greatly reduced.  But DIGITAL
UNIX will always beat Linux, It is closely  coupled with system development.
If you have to think which one you need, Linux should be your choice. You go
to DIGITAL UNIX or HP UNIX when you know what you really need and have the
$$$$ to spend.

And since its only $49 (OK $80 now) If it does not perform as you require,
Buy DIGITAL UNIX + Lic. and Install it on the hardware you already have..  A
real easy upgrade path :^ )  and no risk,. (except for the $49-80) and
relink anything you wrote.

