: Now if they would only release enough libraries so that we could
: get the Tru64 Netscape running and make it trivially obvious
: how to do this . . .

It IS trivially obvious how to do this.  First you buy a license
and from that moment on it is donwhill... :-)

"Tru64 Netscape" actually is not "true64".  It was compiled with '-taso'
(or '-xtaso', or something similar) switch which limits its address space
to 32-bits; precisely to bypass those Netscape bugs which are caused by
assumptions that the whole world is 32-bit.  Nobody ever hacked similar
compiler options on Linux so you are condemned to fixing Mozilla. :-)
Actually if all people clamoring for Netscape on Alpha would chip-in
with that task it likely would be much further ahead.

