From my understanding of things, FX32 allows the use of Intel directed programs
on Alphas when both are running Windows NT as the OS.  Linux is completely
different to Windows NT at the systems level and although FX32 is clever, it is
not clever enough to change system level information as well as machine
instructions - all on the fly.

The Paint Shop Pro downloads that I have used were Windows directed.  I would
like to be proven wrong, but the download you have is most likely both Intel and
Windows directed.  Paint Shop with an X Window interface would be just what the
doctor ordered, but I know of no such beast.

