> I've just installed RedHat 6.0 (kernel 2.0.35) on an AlphaStation 200
> (4/166), and I've got an odd problem that I'm having difficulty figuring
> out (partially due to the nature of the problem).
> 
> I get a login prompt (I'm not using X) and can log in as root.
> 
> Then, about 20-30 seconds later, I am magically booted out, and presented
> with the login prompt again.  This happens at every login attempt, regardless
> of virtual console (i.e. ALT-Fn).

Yes, I had that problem when I upgraded my Multia UDB from RH5.2 to
RH6.0. That was a stressful day :-)

If I remember correctly, the problem was that the UDB's bootloader was
still configured to load the old kernel, which is "vmlinux" (or similar)
in the root directory. I changed the bootloader to point at
"/boot/vmlinuz" (this is a symlink to the new kernel) and it was fine
after that.

Even better, if you compile a new kernel, you just have to update the
symlink and reboot - unlike the i386 where you have to mess around with
LILO :-)

HTH,

Brian.



