I've used a lot of Alpha systems, mainly for development, on OSF, VMS
and NT.

Pros:

- More registers (useful for assembly debugging)
- 64-bit memory addressing (I've used machines with way more than 4 GB)
- 64-bit integers and arithmetic (for those that need it)
- They're a little bit ahead on the power curve.
- Digital has had a tradition of building solid, though somewhat
  proprietary, hardware



