Helmut Katzgraber wrote:
> 
> hi there.
> 
> i have a question: on my alpha running rh 6.0 i can renice jobs to
> nicelevel 20, whereas on an intel with the same os i only can get as
> high
> as 19. has anybody a suggestion how i can renice something to 20 (i.e. i
> want it to comfortably rest while other stuff is running) on rh
> 6.0-intel?
> 
> in fact i just tested it: if i start a job on an intel, and type
> 
>         renice 20 PID
>         top
> 
> top shows only nicelevel 19. the same situation on the alpha gives the
> desired nicelevel 20 when i run top.
> 

Why do you want to nice just to 20? Nice levels are *relative* so, 
except if you have another process 'niced' to 19, your program
"eat" the same cpu load if at level 19 or 20.
IMHO the nice level doesn't fix a cpu % load, just reschedule process
priority, so my personal hint is to use the "standard" 19 level
everywhere.
 
