(1) Did it *ever* show the full 96MB?
(2) Did you simply put 64MB sticks in the second bank of memory?

If (1) is no and (2) is yes, try swapping the banks, i.e., put the denser
memory in Bank 0. If it works, you're done. If it comes up with 0MB main
memory, one of the 4 sticks in the 64MB bank is simply bad.

Couldn't find Avanti TRM, but RAM capacity going from highest to lowest for
Banks 0-n is necessary for most (if not all) motherboards, Alpha or Intel.

Hope this is helpful,
Bill

