sysv@wijnkist.warande.net wrote:
: I want to burn cd's in my AXPpci33 (166mhz). 
: cdrecord dev=1,1,0 -checkdrive works file, 
: but cdrecord dev=1,1,0 speed=4 test.iso 
: wount work. It gives the following error
: cdrecord: Invalid argument. shmget failed

There are three solutions:

a) run all your cdrecord sessions with 'fs=2m' argument
b) change the default FIFO size in the cdrecord source and
   recompile
c) increase the maximum size of the shared memory segment in
   the kernel and recompile the kernel. The file you want to
   change is 'include/asm-alpha/shmparam.h' in the kernel
   source tree; setting SHMMAX to 0xffa000 does the trick 
   for me.

IMHO, (c) is the cleanest solution - but that's a matter of 
personal preference.

/Serge.P

--
