I found my problem...

After looking for vmlinuz.gz, I couldn't find it anywhere on my system.
So, I looked for the uncompressed kernel, and found a symbolic link to it
in the /boot directory.  I changed the boot string to point to this
kernel, and everything is working fine now.  Here's the string I"m using:

boot hda5:/boot/vmlinuz root=/dev/hda5

Red Hat could use some documentation regarding this on their site or in
their documentation.  I'm OK with the fact that the kernel is stored in
the /boot directory and not in the root, but I would expect to see some
documentation stating so.

    Greg Hammond


