Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

Just a few comments

1.
You could use the ARC/Alphabios to make a SMALL approx 3 Meg DOS
partition at the beginning of the Hard Drive. Then you can put MILO
and the kernel Image there later, and configure the Bios to boot from
it. Remember the ARC can only read DOS partitions. ALso the MILO disk
must be DOS formatted for the same reason, assuming you don't have SRM
console, ( which is unlikely since it already has NT on it ).

The kernel image disk, and root disk  can be made using RAWRITE from a
DOS machine

2.
When you boot the kernel it assume the root device is /dev/sda2
so you have to add a root=/dev/<device> if that is not the case on
your system. This had me tearing my hair out, until some fine people
on this NG showed me my error ! 

3.
Read the Alpha addendum to the install manual which is on the CD

4.
Have a look at http://www.alphanlinux.org

5.
Remember to choose exactly the right MILO, and Image for your machine
type.


Good luck ! I got it in the end but it took me a few goes !

