             Linload.exe will load the MILO which is in the same
directory if you don't specify where MILO is or give a wrong path. So in
your situation, linload.exe will load milo without specifying the milo
path.
             If the screen freezes after it shows " swapping to PAL
code", it is the problem of compatibility with your video card. The BIOS
emulation code in MILO supports less video cards than XFree86 does. If
you connect the COM1 to a terminal ( or any computer with a teminal
emulation software such as hyper teminal in Windows 95), you can see
that milo is doing its job well except the video initialization.
            You can try downloading the latest milo, but the best way is
to change the video card.


