    If you want to use floppy to install RedHat 6.0, you can refer to my
homepage,
http://www.iol.unh.edu/linux/alpha/started.html. Find generic.img and
ramdisk.img
in /images in the CD and use rawrite.exe to create the disks.
    Then in milo prompt, enter " boot floppy", it will prompt you   put the
ramdisk.

    As to your problem, MILO has already loaded the kernel, so there is
nothing wrong with milo. In fact, the kernel has been loaded fully. The
problem happened when the kernel was initializing the console device. It
seems that the kernel could not get the read/write permission to the
device. This is weird. I will try to work it out.

    I suggest you use the boot disk and ramdisk in Redhat 5.2. You can
download them  from
ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/distributions/redhat/old-releases/redhat-5.2/alpha/images.

Choose xlt.img as your boot image. You need also get the ramdisk.img to
make the ram disk.

 Xiaozhou Qiu

