Looking at the Hardware Compatibility List for the 164LX (
http://www.digital.com/semiconductor/alpha/alpha-hcl.htm ), it appears that the LX and
SX don't take the same memory.

Specifically, the SX does not want ECC, but the LX *does* want it. It needs 72-bit
DIMMS.

It might be a fluke that PC100 SDRAMs work in the SX, but I made sure I got non-ECC
DIMMs for it. You should try the ECC ones. Of course, finding a sympathetic computer
dealer who's willing to let you experiment and bring the memory back if it doesn't
work might be a bit of a trick.

Hope this helps.

Bill

