Hi, If you have time, you'd better have a look at MILO Howto. It will give you
detailed guide.
For either AlphaBIOS or ARC sole, the command suggested by Marco is correct.
However, I suggest you copy the kernel to the root;
$ cp /boot/vmlinuz-2.2.5-16 /vmlinux.gz;
In the field of OS Options in AlphaBIOS or OSLOADOPTIONS in ARC, pass the
following command:
boot sda2:vmlinux.gz  root=/dev/sda2
For other settings in AlphaBIOS or ARC console, you follow RedHat's guide or
MILO howto. You should be all set.

