AndreHeidenreich <heid.a@swol.de> writes:
> could anyone explain me the following error i get while executing the
> alpha/linux gas with
> 'as -nocpp -o _divdi3.o _divdi3.s' on an rh6.0 alpha/linux?
> 
> _divdi3.s:392: Error: macro requires $at register while noat in effect
>[...]
>         ldbu $1,0($1)                <-- zeile 392

That's a "load byte" instruction which is part of the BWX extension to
the Alpha instruction set.  It only exists on chips from the EV56
onwards.  Your assembler probably assumes EV4.  Try adding the
"-m21164a" flag to the command line.  You can check what your "as"
knows about as follows:

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> strings `which as` | grep -- -m
-m21064 | -m21066 | -m21164 | -m21164a
-mev4 | -mev45 | -mev5 | -mev56 | -mall
-M,--mri
------------------------------------------------------------------------------


By the way, did you encounter the error when trying to build egcs?
If so read the egcs FAQ entry about configuring for alphaev5 instead
of alphaev56, in case it is relevant to you.

Bye,
  Rob.



