when you power -up keep hitting ctrl-c, you should get to the SRM prompt
">>>",

Then type "set auto_action halt" followed by a return. next time you boot,
it should halt to the SRM console prompt.

usually you would set the "boot_device", "boot_file" and "boot_osflags" and
set auto_action to "boot". so when the system is turned on, it will boot
without user intervention.

JJ

