Just brought up a 164SX, so here's what I know:

It takes 168-pin SDRAM DIMMs wo/ECC, which have to be installed in pairs. If you
look to Kingston (or the other name brands) for RAM, they'll take an enormous
amount cash from you (maybe $120/64MB) for what they guarantee to work with the
board, and the DEC compatibility list, which lists a lot of expensive memory,
won't admit the simple truth: PC100 non-ECC SDRAM DIMMs work fine. Going rate on
these is about $50/64MB.

I'm told that PC66 DIMMs do NOT work, even though the RAM is on a 66-Mhz bus. I
don't know why.

Hope this helps.

Bill

