	Christian Hennecke <christian.hennecke@ruhr-uni-bochum.de> writes:

[swap hell in 32 M]

> How many MBs of RAM would you suggest to get a machine running without
> much swapping when using KDE or GNOME w/ Enlightenment as
> Desktopenvironment?

I use a 96 meg AS200 with Windowmaker and it's okay.  Adding all that
desktop cruft will drive memory requirements up - especially on an
Alpha.  For what you're proposing I'd say that 96 megs is a minimum
RAM size I'd try for the system to run smoothly.  If you go for less
memory, you'd probably do better dropping to a lighter desktop.  KDE
was okay when I had 80 megs, but was downright painful at 40 if you
actually wanted to use an application rather than just play with the
desktop. :).

