In article <3788DFAE.C2D2EF5F@technologist.com>, Scott
<scott4000@technologist.com> wrote:

:    What are the advantages and disadvantages of using Linux over Tru64
:(Digital UNIX) for an Alpha 21264 system?

Top three reasons for Linux over Tru64:

1. Linux is cheaper.
2. Linux is cheaper.
3. Linux is cheaper.

Believe me, Tru64 is EXPENSIVE, at least if you get all the bells and
whistles for an unlimited SMP license.  Our dual-processor 21264 with 1GB
RAM cost about $14000--and Tru64 doubled the price.

But you really need to supplement the Digital UNIX with the GNU versions
of utilities.  I got used to doing a "grep" with leading and/or trailing
context that I couldn't believe that isn't part of the standard grep;
sadly, it's true.

I look forward to the Linux versions of the Tru64 compilers.  What you're
willing to pay for a server may be quite different from what you're
willing to pay for your desktop workstation.

--Ron Bruck



