I was also having this problem. I dont know if it existed in the
distributed RH6 kernel (2.2.5). As soon as I upgraded to 2.2.7, NFS
serving broke. So, I started digging into the problem when I upgraded
again to 2.2.10. Voila -- if at the beginning of the config (sorry, I
always use 'make config') you dont say Y to "experimental/development
options", then you will *NEVER* be prompted for CONFIG_NFSD (not
CONFIG_NFS, which is the client side!).

So, say Y to the development/experimental options, and then configure as
you normally would. When you get to the filesystems part, you *WILL* be
prompted for both NFS client (CONFIG_NFS) and NFS Server (CONFIG_NFSD).
Say 'Y' (or 'm') for CONFIG_NFSD, and you'll be on your way.

I have no idea if this is also the case with x86 (still running RH5.2
there).

					/AWF

