Hi folks,

This box is about to go into use by the bioperl
project, http://bio.perl.org. I've been using alpha's
for a while now (2100's, 4100's and 8400's) but this
is the first linux install on Alpha I've done.

Summary:

Cannot access TLZ10 DAT drive as a device,
looking for all possible hints, pointers, URL's etc....

Gory details:

Right after my 600a box showed up I grabbed
a TLZ10 DAT drive, set the SCSI ID to '5' with
the jumpers and wired it into the chassis.

The RH5.2 installation went fine and the tape
drive was recognized throughout the process.

The problem is that I cannot actually access
the tape drive as a device within unix. dump, mt, tar, etc.
all fail to work.

Here is the output from /proc/scsi/scsi
=======================================
Attached devices:
Host: scsi0 Channel: 00 Id: 00 Lun: 00
  Vendor: DEC      Model: RZ1CC-BA (C) DEC Rev: 883F
  Type:   Direct-Access                    ANSI SCSI revision: 02
Host: scsi0 Channel: 00 Id: 01 Lun: 00
  Vendor: DEC      Model: RZ1CC-BA (C) DEC Rev: 883F
  Type:   Direct-Access                    ANSI SCSI revision: 02
Host: scsi0 Channel: 00 Id: 05 Lun: 00
  Vendor: DEC      Model: TLZ10    (C) DEC Rev: 04a8
  Type:   Sequential-Access                ANSI SCSI revision: 02
========================================

The tape drive is certainly present :) I just cannot
seem to access it.

I'm at a loss as to what to try next. I'm not sure if I
have a MAKEDEV problem, a kernel issue or possibly even a
bad drive. Am I correct in thinking that this device should
be /dev/st0 and /dev/nst0?

There does not seem to be much in the way of SCSI stuff
in the FAQ and HowTo sections. Any info or tips on how
I can tackle this problem would be appreciated.

-chris




