>It would be great if VMware would port their software to Alpha also.
>You could have:
>
>1) great FP performance and all the Unix utilities on Alpha Linux
>2) native Alpha CPU office applications under Win NT
>3) emulated x86 applications using FX32!
>
>The only thing I'm not sure about is whether the Alpha CPU has
>anything similar to virtual mode on the x86.

No, but it doesn't need one.  The only thing virtual-8086 mode can
virtualize is real mode software; since no the alpha does not have
multiple modes of operation (other than user/kernel (and a couple more
if you use VMS PALcode)), it doesn't need to virtualize them.

The main problem in writing vmware-like software for the alpha is that
you'd have to emulate the PALcode of the guest OS; it should be
possible, but probably not too easy, and not all OSes use the same
PALcode.  I'm not aware of any problems virtualizing kernel mode on the
alpha like those on the x86, but there may be some.

