I eventually tried RH 6.0 the last night and the problem, which showed
up on my setup with a freshly installed set of 6.0 with updates, turned
out to be utterly trivial.  Somebody forgot to add a line like:

none          /dev/pts     devpts   defaults 0 0

in /etc/fstab (don't forget to mount that explicitely if not rebooting
and you may achieve the same effect in a couple of other ways). Without
this pseudo-terminals are missing and xterm from 6.0, for example, wants
them really badly. :-)


: :> is
: :> > brought down and then restarted, the manager fails with the message:
: :> >   _FontTransSocketUNIXConnection: Can't connect: eror = 61
: :> >   failed to set default font path 'unix/1:-1'
: :> >   Fatal server error: could not open default font 'fixed'.

Number of people reported that.  Using an explicit font path instead of
a font server (edit XF86Config) is maybe less elegant and not that
flexible but it works. :-)

